body:
Shouldnt the undefined index throw a notice. That would render your example invalid.

Alternatively you could use the array syntax in those cases where the first argument is null:

``` php
echo __('Your %s appointment for %s is confirmed!', array(
    null,
    $notNull
));
```

@AD7six With respect to speed, I agree. I'd even go so far as remove the variable arguments and force an array parameter. (with so many breaking changes to Cake3, now would be a good time :))

`$args = array_slice(func_get_args(), 1);` can't be helping performance -- and this is the default code path. ( I only noticed the array signature when I looked at the code. The Book doesn't mention it so most devs don't use the array input:
http://book.cakephp.org/2.0/en/core-libraries/global-constants-and-functions.html#__ )

Where would I put the corresponding benchmark in a testcase for a pull request?
- And it really is a few lines testprogramm to see my statement about the evaluation of the other operand:

```
function i_will_exit() { exit; }
if(false && i_will_exit()) {
  echo "I will never be shown, because i_will_exit() has been called beforehand.";
} else {
  echo "if i_will_exit() would have been called, you would not read this!";
}
```

I hope you can see the point here. If you tell me where to correctly append a benchmark in a testcase, I wil provide one!
